„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sectionsœ…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMSpeak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, I am the LORD your God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆAfter the doings of the land of Egypt, wherein ye dwelt, shall ye not do: and after the doings of the land of Canaan, whither I bring you, shall ye not do: neither shall ye walk in their ordinances.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Ye shall do my judgments, and keep mine ordinances, to walk therein: I am the LORD your God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoYe shall therefore keep my statutes, and my judgments: which if a man do, he shall live in them: I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhNone of you shall approach to any that is near of kin to him, to uncover their nakedness: I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe nakedness of thy father, or the nakedness of thy mother, shalt thou not uncover: she is thy mother; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXThe nakedness of thy father's wife shalt thou not uncover: it is thy father's nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­The nakedness of thy sister, the daughter of thy father, or daughter of thy mother, whether she be born at home, or born abroad, even their nakedness thou shalt not uncover.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”The nakedness of thy son's daughter, or of thy daughter's daughter, even their nakedness thou shalt not uncover: for their's is thine own nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe nakedness of thy father's wife's daughter, begotten of thy father, she is thy sister, thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father's sister: she is thy father's near kinswoman.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdThou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy mother's sister: for she is thy mother's near kinswoman.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father's brother, thou shalt not approach to his wife: she is thine aunt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy daughter in law: she is thy son's wife; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZThou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy brother's wife: it is thy brother's nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖThou shalt not uncover the nakedness of a woman and her daughter, neither shalt thou take her son's daughter, or her daughter's daughter, to uncover her nakedness; for they are her near kinswomen: it is wickedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvNeither shalt thou take a wife to her sister, to vex her, to uncover her nakedness, beside the other in her life time.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAlso thou shalt not approach unto a woman to uncover her nakedness, as long as she is put apart for her uncleanness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Moreover thou shalt not lie carnally with thy neighbour's wife, to defile thyself with her.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And thou shalt not let any of thy seed pass through the fire to Molech, neither shalt thou profane the name of thy God: I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFThou shalt not lie with mankind, as with womankind: it is abomination.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•Neither shalt thou lie with any beast to defile thyself therewith: neither shall any woman stand before a beast to lie down thereto: it is confusion.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvDefile not ye yourselves in any of these things: for in all these the nations are defiled which I cast out before you:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}and the land is defiled: therefore I do visit the iniquity thereof upon it, and the land itself vomiteth out her inhabitants.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±Ye shall therefore keep my statutes and my judgments, and shall not commit any of these abominations; neither any of your own nation, nor any stranger that sojourneth among you:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙk(for all these abominations have the men of the land done, which were before you, and the land is defiled;)¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙithat the land spue not you out also, when ye defile it, as it spued out the nations that were before you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor whosoever shall commit any of these abominations, even the souls that commit them shall be cut off from among their people.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃTherefore shall ye keep mine ordinance, that ye commit not any one of these abominable customs, which were committed before you, and that ye defile not yourselves therein: I am the LORD your God.¦layout ªlast_verse